I need a haircut.
I call a local salon.
A woman answers the phone.
"Hello, welcome to the salon," she says.
"Hello, I need a haircut on Saturday," I say.
"Yes Madam, there is time on Saturday," she says.
"What time do you have available?" I ask.
"We always open the salon at nine in the morning," she explains.
"The time at ten o'clock or eleven o'clock on Saturday morning is free."
I look at my calendar.
"Saturday morning at eleven o'clock is absolutely fine," I say.
"Okay Madam, eleven o'clock in the morning."
"What is your name?" she asks.
"My name is Maya," I reply.
"Thank you Maya Madam, your appointment is booked," she says.
"Thank you very much," I say.
I hang up the phone.
I do not get my hair cut every day.
I only go to the salon sometimes.
Now my Saturday is set.
